GAPS FOUND, BOTH FIXED:
1. #1641 literal net names in the GUI PLAN's selection (fixed 78d12283).
   b238a0b6 made expand_net_patterns pass the board's names to
   net_pattern_matches, so on the CLI a pattern with no '*'/'?' that spells a
   net ('D[3]') selects that net only; ai_plan._match_net_names did not pass
   them, so 'D[3]' selected [/D3, /D[3]] in the plan and '!D[3]' dropped /D3.
   The route_diff step's pair match used fnmatch. Both now use the CLIs'
   matcher with the board's names; test_1641_plan_literal_net_names compares
   the plan with expand_net_patterns (5 checks fail without the fix).
2. Net-filtered keep-outs on the plane step (fixed daa77a46). #1760/#1778's
   gate reads pcb_data._net_keepouts, which create_plane never attached: the
   CLI's route_planes (and its GND-via block, a second fresh parse) never
   honoured a net-filtered .kicad_dru keep-out, and the Planes tab honoured
   one only when an earlier Route/Differential run had left the list on its
   long-lived PCBData. create_plane and the CLI's GND-via block now attach
   (or clear) the board's own list, as repair_planes does.
   test_create_plane_net_keepouts (CLI, its via landed inside before) and
   test_gnd_vias_gui's new net keep-out arm (both fronts keep out and place
   the same vias; the tab lands inside with create_plane's attach removed).

